### 4. Constructions  

#### 4.1  \(k=0\)

> “Take the vertical lines \(x=1,\dots ,x=n\). … every point \((a,b)\in T_n\) lies on the line \(x=a\).”

- **Verification:** Correct; all lines are non‑sunny, exactly \(n\) distinct lines, covering all points. No issue.

#### 4.2  \(k=1\)

> “Use the \(n-1\) vertical lines \(x=1,\dots ,x=n-1\) together with the sunny line  
