  - The remaining columns \(1\) through \(n-3\) are each covered by a distinct vertical line, giving a total of \((n-3)+3=n\) distinct lines, exactly three of which are sunny.  
  - All lines are distinct and satisfy the “sunny” condition where required. Construction is valid.

